### Vendored marketing skills library

The distribution bundles a **pinned copy of a third-party marketing skills
library**. It is redistributed, and its licence is recorded here in full
because the licence requires exactly that.

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Upstream project | **Marketing Skills** by Corey Haines |
| Repository | `https://github.com/coreyhaines31/marketingskills` |
| Release tag | **`v2.11.1`** |
| Pinned commit | **`5b2c0007766c6a1cf1d53fd8fc73e979e0821022`** |
| License | **MIT** |
| Copyright | `Copyright (c) 2025 Corey Haines` |
| Vendored path | `.agents/skills/` (the library only) |
| Vendored license text | `.agents/LICENSE` — the upstream `LICENSE` **verbatim** at the pinned commit |

MIT requires only that "the above copyright notice and this permission notice
shall be included in all copies or substantial portions of the Software". That
is why the upstream `LICENSE` file itself is shipped, byte-for-byte, next to the
library — in the Windows installer payload (via `packaging/omos.spec` `datas`)
and in the public repository (via `scripts/package/export_public_repo.py`).

**This library is not modified.** The vendored copy is content-identical to
upstream `v2.11.1` after line-ending normalization; the integrity record is
`skills-lock.json` plus `docs/marketing-skills-manifest.json`, and it is
re-verified rather than asserted.

`.agents/product-marketing.md` is **not** part of the upstream library. It is
OMOS-authored, it is licensed Apache-2.0 like the rest of this project, and it
contains a named third party's Marketing Brain material. It is not
redistributed, and the MIT grant recorded above does not cover it. See
`docs/opensource/license-audit.md`.

